                   'People living near these mountains may show respect through prayers, offerings, and '
                   'local religious customs. These beliefs connect the spiritual world with the natural '
                   'environment.\n'
                   '\n'
                   'In Himalayan belief, the name Jomo can refer to different revered female figures, '
                   'and stories vary by locality. Sacred mountains may be understood as more than '
                   'physical landmarks: they can also be places of spiritual presence and communal '
                   'memory. It is important not to combine the separate legends of different Jomo '
                   'deities into a single invented biography.\n'
                   '\n'
                   'The title Jomo is encountered in more than one Himalayan religious and local '
